From dbad59e33050939d90f150270ba4314f0dafc86d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homelab <homelab@emrys.dev>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:56:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] core: scope the admin, crawl and progress querysets

get_queryset() on the snapshot, archive-result, crawl and schedule admins
carries the same forced filter as the views, which covers the changelist,
its search, its filters and every bulk action. A change-form id that is out
of scope answers 404 rather than the admin's "does not exist" redirect, and
custom admin views resolve through the scoped queryset.

ONLY_NEW de-duplication becomes per owner: another user's capture of a URL
must not make your add a no-op. Tag cards, counts and exports are scoped
for the same reason a shared tag is on everyone's captures.
